    "explanation": "This case goes to a human reviewer. The 5.00 SGD cancellation fee is held: it is neither paid to the driver nor finally returned to the rider, and no outcome is inferred from the gap in the record (POL-GEN-26; ESCALATE is terminal under POL-GEN-03).\n\nSettled facts. The driver reached the pickup: the trip record's arrival event at 11:11:50 is corroborated by the GPS trace under POL-NS-21 (nearest fix 2.05 m from the pickup, reported accuracy 5 m, comfortably inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius). The trip was on-demand with no scheduled time, so the 300-second free wait ran from arrival and expired at 11:16:50; the driver cancelled at 11:18:10, 380 seconds after arrival (POL-NS-21). The call half of the driver's contact duty under POL-NS-23 is met: one in-app call at 11:14:20, unanswered after 20 s, before cancellation.\n\nThe undecided fact. POL-NS-23 also requires at least one in-app chat message from the driver before cancelling. The only artifact that could carry it is the chat log, EV-CHAT-05065, and it is impaired: issue code TRUNCATED_LOG at weight 0.6 — it exports 1 of the 3 entries the trip record counts, with nothing after 11:06:00, so the arrival and the entire six-minute waiting window are missing. That missing stretch is exactly where a driver message would sit. An impaired record cannot be read as proof that no message was sent, so the message limb is undecided, not failed — it supports neither the payment the driver wants nor the refund the rider wants.\n\nRider: your request that the fee be treated as void (full refund / NO_ACTION) because the message limb is 'not met' is not accepted. It is true the exported log shows no driver message, but the log is incomplete over the very window in question, so it establishes neither a message nor its absence. POL-GEN-26 names this exact fact — whether the driver messaged and called before cancelling — as one that, when it cannot be established because the evidence is impaired, sends the case to a human reviewer and forbids an outcome being inferred from the absence, and POL-NS-26 makes the AI's finality on a no-show subject to POL-GEN-26. Your counter-statement (no message, only a missed call) has been read, but POL-NS-23's test is the chat log and the call record, not a party's account, so it does not decide the limb.\n\nDriver: your request for DRIVER_COMPENSATION of 5.00 SGD is not accepted either. POL-NS-22 transfers the fee to you only where the fee stands, and it cannot stand while the contact obligation is unresolved. The 5.00 SGD is exactly the policy figure, so no fee-amount referral arises under POL-NS-22, and EV-FARE-05065 records 5.00 SGD already refunded to the rider and withheld from you at 13:59:10.\n\nReferrals: none. POL-NS-25 does not fire (the rider's profile snapshot does not carry no_show_cancellations_30d, and the fee does not stand), and POL-NS-24's goodwill credit does not apply (on-demand trip with no scheduled time, and the cancellation was the driver's, not the rider's).\n\nOpen question for the reviewer, belonging here and not in referrals: whether the driver sent at least one in-app chat message before 11:18:10, to be resolved from the unexported chat entries.\n\nConfidence 0.6, capped by the impaired chat log (EV-CHAT-05065, TRUNCATED_LOG, weight 0.6) that this finding rests on. Under POL-GEN-22 and POL-NS-26 the amount in dispute (5.00 SGD) is below the 10.00 SGD band and neither party carries a fraud flag, so no higher confidence bar applies."
  },
